On Friday, August 8, 2014 4:12:32 AM UTC-7, Jakub Nowak wrote:
> Hello  everyone,
>
> I am trying to generate heatmaps for my data and run in following problems. I would be grateful for some suggestions about heat map code.
>
> I arranged matrix for the heatmap by myself and I would like to keep this not changed during heat map plotting. I tried both heatmap.2 (gplot) and geom_tile (ggplot2) with no luck to get what I want. heatmap.2 keeps the sort but layout is bad and ggplot2 reorganises data in the heat map.
>
> Can you suggest how to switch off clustering in ggplot2?
>
> Here is the code I used.
>
> Generating heatmap with ggplot2
>
> ```{r}
> if (!require("reshape2")) {
> install.packages("reshape2", dependencies = TRUE)
> library(reshape2)
> }
> if (!require("plyr")) {
> install.packages("plyr", dependencies = TRUE)
> library(plyr)
> }
> if (!require("scales")) {
> install.packages("scales", dependencies = TRUE)
> library(scales)
> }
> if (!require("ggplot2")) {
> install.packages("ggplot2", dependencies = TRUE)
> library(ggplot2)
> }
> data.sorted.merged.test <- data.sorted.merged[,-c(2:5,8)]
> data.heatmap2 <- melt(data.sorted.merged.test)
> data.heatmap2 <- ddply(data.heatmap2, .(variable), transform,rescale = rescale(value))
> ggplot(data.heatmap2, aes(variable, ID))+ geom_tile(aes(fill=rescale), colour="white") +
>  scale_fill_gradient(low="white", high="red", breaks=colbreaks)
> ```
>
> Also I can attach png files of the heat map if that can help.
>
> Thanks very much for your help,
>
> Jakub

